==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|caput|caput|the head}}. {{doublet|en|head}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkæpət/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|capita}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy}} The [[head]].
# {{lb|en|anatomy}} A [[knob]]-like [[protuberance]] or [[capitulum]].
# The [[top]] or [[superior]] part of a thing.
# {{lb|en|UK}} The [[council]] or ruling body of the University of [[Cambridge]] prior to the constitution of 1856.
#* Lamb
#*: Your '''caputs''' and heads of colleges.
# {{lb|en|medicine|colloquial}} {{short for|caput succedaneum|lang=en}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|caput mortuum}}

